# data.db was tracked with Git LFS until commit 8315804 ("chore: stop tracking
# data.db"); it is now in .gitignore and no longer in the tree. The rule is kept
# as a record rather than deleted: it explains why a clone of this repository
# once pulled gigabytes of LFS objects that no current commit references.
# Measured 2026-09-20: `git lfs ls-files` returns nothing, and `git lfs prune`
# freed 2.6 GB of orphaned local cache. If data.db is ever tracked again, this
# line is already correct.
data.db filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# This module's Go sources are LF in the index and must be LF in the worktree
# too. gofmt compares the bytes ON DISK, so a CRLF checkout makes `gofmt -l`
# list a file that is byte-identical to a clean one. Measured on
# pubvera-trialvera's providers.go: gofmt listed it, the file had CRLF endings,
# and CI on Linux passed green — a false positive that costs a diagnosis every
# time it fires. eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf=true, which put the CRLF there.
*.go text eol=lf

# Both vendored CLIs are tracked with Git LFS. git cannot delta-compress a
# ~20 MB binary between versions, so every vendoring added another full copy to
# the history permanently. Measured on 2026-09-20: 12 blobs of
# thelancet-pp-cli-linux and 8 of retraction-checker-pp-cli-linux, packed
# repository at 62 MiB after gc.
#
# LFS stores a ~130 byte pointer in the commit and keeps the binary outside the
# object database, so a clone fetches the current versions instead of all twenty.
#
# -text is explicit rather than left to content sniffing: neither file has an
# extension, and a single converted byte would corrupt the ELF silently.
#
# retraction-checker-pp-cli-linux is also vendored into pubvera-retractis, and
# neither LFS nor gc can deduplicate across repositories. Do NOT compare the two
# copies by sha256: a differing hash does not mean differing code. The build is
# -trimpath deterministic, but the Go BuildID's FIRST segment is an action ID
# that takes the build directory into account, and this repo compiles in
# cli-src-retraction while retractis uses its own. Compare the THIRD BuildID
# segment instead — that one identifies the compiled code — together with the
# byte size and the Go version:
#   file bin/retraction-checker-pp-cli-linux
# An earlier version of this comment quoted the two sha256 prefixes and called
# the copies different builds. That was true at the time for a different reason
# (this copy predated upstream #1978) and became misleading the moment it was
# revendored, which is why the numbers are gone and the method is here instead.
# Keeping the two in step remains a separate open question.
#
# This stops future growth only. The twenty blobs already in the history stay
# where they are: removing them means rewriting history, which invalidates every
# existing clone and every commit hash. That is a separate decision.
#
# Anyone checking out this repository needs git-lfs installed. CI already checks
# out with lfs: true.
bin/thelancet-pp-cli-linux filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
bin/retraction-checker-pp-cli-linux filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text